	including `<helix/raylib/shaders/lights.glsl>`: rlights' uniforms and `vec4 helixLight(vec4 texelColor, vec4 tint, vec3
	fragPosition, vec3 fragNormal)`, called as `helixLight(texture(texture0, fragTexCoord), colDiffuse*fragColor, fragPosition,
	fragNormal)`; and as the PBR one does by including `<helix/raylib/shaders/pbr.glsl>`, `vec4 helixPbr(vec4 baseColor, float metallic,
	float roughness, float occlusion, vec3 emissive, vec3 fragPosition, vec3 normal)`. A program that calls none of this links none of
	it.

	Shadows:

	```haxe
	var pbr = LoadPbrShader();
	var sun = CreateLight(LIGHT_DIRECTIONAL, new Vector3(4, 10, 2), Vector3Zero(), WHITE, pbr);
	SetLightShadows(pbr, sun, {mapSize: 2048, distance: 30});
	// each frame
	BeginShadowMode(pbr, sun, camera);
	DrawModel(island, Vector3Zero(), 1, WHITE);
	DrawModel(hut, hutPosition, 1, WHITE);
	EndShadowMode();
	BeginMode3D(camera);
	DrawModel(island, Vector3Zero(), 1, WHITE);
	DrawModel(hut, hutPosition, 1, WHITE);
	EndMode3D();
	```

	A light casts shadows once `SetLightShadows` turns them on. Each frame its shadows are what was drawn in its shadow pass, between
	`BeginShadowMode` and `EndShadowMode`. A frame without the pass keeps the shadows of the last one. Every draw through the shader
	receives them: `LoadPbrShader`'s and `LoadLightingShader`'s, and a program's own that includes `<helix/raylib/shaders/shadows.glsl>`
	and calls `float helixShadow(int light, vec3 fragPosition, vec3 fragNormal)`, 0 in full shadow to 1 in full light. A directional
	light's shadows follow the camera, and a point light's fall every way from it.

	A shader compiled by `CompileShaderFile` carries its shadow variant: its own vertex stage, with a fragment stage writing depth alone
	and cutting at the material's alpha cutoff. The shadow pass draws through it. */
